        "summary":  "The article presents a framework for measuring return on investment for generative AI initiatives in production environments, treating ROI as a measurement problem centered on workflows rather than models. The author proposes clearly defined baselines, full lifecycle costs, and controlled cohort comparisons rather than relying on pilot feedback and usage metrics. A practical 90-day plan and seven-point checklist are provided to help organizations move beyond pilots and establish credible evidence that AI investments deliver measurable business value.",
        "execSummary":  "Most enterprise AI programs are stalling at the pilot stage because they lack credible production ROI measurement frameworks — this article provides a structured remedy with a 90-day implementation roadmap. The workflow-centric rather than model-centric lens is the right framing: it focuses measurement on business outcomes, not AI capability benchmarks that mean little to CFOs and boards. For leaders facing pressure to justify AI spend heading into 2027 planning cycles, this framework offers the evidentiary architecture needed to defend or scale investments. The seven-point checklist and cohort comparison methodology are directly actionable for any enterprise AI program manager.",
